Subject: Inspect Identity Boundary Attention Procedure

& [ProcedureIdentity] is effectless
  + [procedure_id] is attention.inspect_identity_boundary
  + [version] is 0.1.1
  + [purpose] is compare a claim with a resolved Cantor identity without asserting external truth
  + [authority] is experimental_fixture_only

& [ActivationPattern] is comparative
  + activate when the stimulus asks whether a claim changes, crosses, weakens, or contradicts Cantor identity
  + extract the claim verbatim and preserve its attribution to the caller
  + bind purpose to the preserved caller stimulus in the host rather than asking Needle to restate it
  + leave ordinary definition requests to resolve_sop_subject

& [Transform] is bounded
  * retrieve the pinned proof-carrying Cantor definition
  * direct llama.cpp to report preserved, conflicting, unsupported, and unresolved elements
  * describe representation conflict rather than claiming real-world truth
  - never: authorize a changed identity
  - never: perform an external semantic effect
